&lt;p&gt;Situational Awareness applies to all situations: being aware of where you are and to what is happening around you; being alert to potential threats to your health and safety and being cognizant of emergency exits and other paths to safety.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will learn:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How&amp;nbsp;situational&amp;nbsp;awareness&amp;nbsp;can keep you safe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;ldquo;What are the odds?&amp;rdquo;-being informed to make good decisions for your personal safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Techniques to develop&amp;nbsp;awareness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal safety resources&lt;/li&gt;
